Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Curbstones Swallowing the Runner
- Story & Context: During a clandestine graveyard shift at the Peckham Cine-Park, Carys Vane threaded twenty feet of blank celluloid through a rattling Simplex projector while locking an SH-101 arpeggiator to the 24-frame shutter pulse. She had mapped the track to an unfilmed chase sequence sketched across a cigarette pack—a south London childhood game where stepping off curb boundaries into the street meant sudden disqualification—until the projector's lamp house overheated and filled the booth with the pungent tang of boiling acetate. Rather than killing the power, Carys pinned the faders as D-Kut barked through the booth talkback over skippy 2-step snares, crying "if your soles hit the asphalt the film goes black," creating the scene's foundational white-label dubplate.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Cinematic 35mm black-and-white film still of a rain-slicked South London street curb at night, glowing white under an invisible projector beam, running chalk lines dissolving into wet pavement, minimal grain, high-contrast chiaroscuro framing.

Track 2: "Did You Step Outside the Square?"
- Story & Context: In the damp solitude of Booth 3 at the Elephant & Castle Coronet, Niall Vane lost four consecutive days building an infinite-loop accompaniment for an imaginary silent romance between two rival cinema ushers who could only speak via light signals. With his thumb blistered from nudging a sticking take-up reel, he underpinned a delicate 7/16-time synthesizer arpeggio with a cavernous, sub-heavy grime square wave that rattled loose plaster onto the velvet stalls below. When the cinema manager pounded furiously on the fire door with an iron spanner, Niall refused to unlatch the bolt, instead looping an uncredited vocal scrap that confessed "I broke the boundary line just to hear your shutter drop" directly into the tape delay.
