Track 3: Carys Vane at the Coronet Gate
- Story & Context: Long after the Coronet was boarded up ahead of demolition, urban explorers claimed that local pirate transmissions on 104.4 FM were still broadcasting an uncatalogued Lantern Guild live take directly from the basement reel-storage vault. The recording captured Carys alone at dawn, feeding contact-mic recordings of the theater's rusting exterior turnstiles into a cascading, trance-like Korg arpeggio that dissolved into cavernous garage swing. The mythology of the scene was sealed when the transmission ended abruptly on an eerie, clipped vocal refrain insisting "the credits roll but nobody leaves the room," right as bailiffs breached the perimeter and found only an idling car battery wired to an empty tape deck.
